  "id": "perseveration",
  "term": "perseveration",
  "definition": "In this historical psychology usage, perseveration refers to an experience that has just occurred remaining, in a special way, still present and held for examination rather than being reconstructed by later reflection. It contrasts with indirect recollection, in which the experience must be reproduced in memory for inspection.",
